# The zoo's captures are a byte-for-byte copy, and `tests/test_zoo.py`
# re-derives each file's sha256 against the zoo's sealed manifests. `-text`
# turns off every line-ending conversion a checkout could apply to them.
fixtures/zoo/** -text
# The raw bodies are the exporter's protobuf, not text: `binary` also keeps
# them out of textual diffs and merges.
fixtures/zoo/**/raw/*.body binary
# The review archives are kept byte for byte, and `tests/test_doc_truth.py`
# hashes each one's bytes against the sha256 TASKS.md records for it. Without
# `-text`, a `core.autocrlf=true` checkout writes CRLF and every archive's
# digest is red on that machine alone.
reviews/** -text
